{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-adelic-tate-motivic-dual","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:adelic-tate-motivic-dual","kind":"remark","title":"Motivic dual of the adelic zeta factorisation via the arc space and motivic measure","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-arc-space","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-adelic-tate-squeeze","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-bsd-surreal-bound"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-arc-space","cites":["references/kontsevich1995","references/denef-loeser2001"],"tags":["adeles","motivic-integration","arc-space","tate-thesis","surreal"],"text":"adelic-tate-motivic-dual.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:adelic-tate-motivic-dual\"></a><p><strong>Motivic dual.</strong> The adelic decomposition of the global zeta integral has a geometric dual via the arc space <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}(X)</code> and the Kontsevich--Denef--Loeser motivic measure. Motivic integration on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}(X)</code> factorises a class in the Grothendieck ring of varieties as a sum over jet-scheme cylinders.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/adelic-tate-motivic-dual.md","heading":"Remark","number":"21.5.10","page":"b/rem-adelic-tate-motivic-dual","qa":{"counts":{"pass":59,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
